# Discord patch notes

Until the user explicitly says to ship, draft patch notes in chat or wiki as pending. Do not post Discord "this is live" notes.

Whenever Bonesaw, Living Gear, or playerbots features actually ship, include a short Discord-ready patch notes bullet list in the reply.

- Player-facing only: no file paths, no spell IDs unless a player needs them
- ASCII-friendly plain `-` bullets, grouped by theme
- Title: `Bonesaw X.Y.Z - patch notes` from `tools/client-update/Bonesaw.version` after bumping it for this ship
- Bump `Bonesaw.version` on every ship, including server-only, so launcher and Discord stay aligned. Do not skip numbers.
- List only what is actually in worldserver or the client; omit in-progress work
- Bold sparingly if Discord-flavored markdown helps
- Keep it simple and paste-ready for their Discord channel
- Extra jump is disabled; do not advertise it
- Append durable learnings to `A:\obsidian\jeremy\wiki\Bonesaw.md` (crashes, UI, deploy, spell IDs); ASCII-only client strings
